  message: "DONE in PR #1874 (merged, dev 1b50a90482). Root cause: the magnet detector read \"was the target type identified\" from a hand-written subset of meta['receiver'] values that never gained declared_type. Fix: the subset is now RECEIVER_IDENTIFIES_TARGET, a mapping that places all 11 written values (identified: typed_var, typed_field, field_chain, declared_type, self, external, constant_external, stdlib, qualified; receiver-blind: bare, generic). test_receiver_vocabulary_partition walks every analyzer source (AST) and fails on a written value the mapping does not place and on a placed value nothing writes, with a positive control. Ruby checked: 'self' binds only the enclosing class's own method (identified); 'generic' binds Const.m but also Const.other(..).m (kept blind); 'bare' kept blind.\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, the filed repro re-run on merged dev: `hypergumbo survey` on `class Logger { public: void Close() {} void Flush() {} }; class App { public: void run() { Logger lg; lg.Close(); lg.Flush(); } };` exit 0 -> App::run -> cpp:app.cpp:1-1:Logger..Close:method 0.85 (was cpp:external:0-0:Close:unresolved 0.4), Flush unchanged at 0.85. Production-path test: test_magnet_demotion_keeps_typed_binds.py::test_cpp_declared_type_receiver_keeps_its_bind.\nMEASURED (published graph re-checked under the old rule): bento4 251 published C++ binds the old rule demoted, all declared_type; spot-checked WriteAdtsHeader's output->Write on an AP4_ByteStream* parameter -> AP4_ByteStream::Write, correct. Registry and spec prose for the receiver key corrected (8 of 11 values listed, Swift missing as a producer, 'no consumer branches on it' false); the key's two-axes leak stays WI-mujug's."  # 5980
